      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "They won't be winning the 955m challenge here with the race now over 1000m but THE SPEED MACHINE (6) has lived up to his name so far with three very good runs to date, a dominant winner on debut at Morphettville then good again at Mornington. He was sent out odds-on favourite in a rich race at Bendigo before a break and this looks right up his alley fresh. SPEIR (1) resumes. He won easily fresh as favourite first up last campaign and is an out-and-out short course horse. Off a long break so watch betting. JENNYANYDOTS (2) can mix her form a bit but has ability and it is very noteworthy she's a synthetic winner at Ballarat over this distance. Will be flashing late. MR TICKLES (4) is also one with synthetic form, mainly at Ballarat but he does boast a second over this trip. He can bounce back.",
